---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service - Geary"
  description="Terms of Service and unofficial disclaimer for Geary, the student-managed BulSU article hub."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 sm:py-10 lg:px-8 lg:py-12">
    <div class="mb-8 border-b border-border-subtle pb-6 max-w-[65ch]">
      <Breadcrumbs
        items={[
          { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
          { label: 'Terms of Service' },
        ]}
      />

      <h1 class="font-heading text-[1.75rem] sm:text-[2.25rem] font-bold leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink-primary">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-3 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-secondary">
        Rules and limitations governing your use of Geary’s student-managed articles.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 text-xs font-medium text-ink-secondary">
        Effective Date: November 19, 2026
      </p>
    </div>

    <article class="geary-prose">
      <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using Geary, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, please discontinue using this website.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Unofficial Status &amp; Non-Affiliation</h2>
      <p>
        Geary is an independent, student-managed information hub created for Bulacan State University (BulSU) students. It is <strong>not</strong> an official publication of, endorsed by, or affiliated with Bulacan State University, its administration, or any official university office.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Informational Purpose Only</h2>
      <p>
        All articles, checklists, fee summaries, grade rules, interactive <a href="/map">Main Campus map</a> layouts, and building or office locations on Geary are provided strictly for general reference. University policies, academic calendars, fees, campus directories, and office locations change without prior notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Always verify critical requirements, deadlines, and official rulings directly with the BulSU Office of the University Registrar, Admissions Office, Office of Student Affairs and Services (OSAS), or your college dean’s office before acting.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>
        You may browse, read, and share links to Geary articles for personal and academic reference. You agree not to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Misrepresent Geary content as official BulSU policy or administration advice.</li>
        <li>Attempt to disrupt hosting infrastructure, overload static endpoints, or scrape content in a way that degrades availability for other students.</li>
        <li>Republish Geary’s article text commercially without attribution.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Content Accuracy, Submissions &amp; Takedowns</h2>
      <p>
        Original article summaries, formatting, and site code belong to Geary’s contributors. Official university names, building names, and policy references remain the property of Bulacan State University or their respective owners. If you spot outdated information or have a correction/removal request, please submit it through the <a href="/contribute">Contribute</a> page or the project’s repository.
      </p>
      <p>
        By submitting an article draft, update, or topic suggestion via <a href="/contribute">/contribute</a>, you confirm that any original text you wrote may be reviewed, edited for clarity and accuracy, published, and updated by Geary maintainers on a non-exclusive, royalty-free basis (with optional credit if provided), and that your submission relies on public official sources rather than unauthorized third-party content.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Disclaimer of Warranties &amp; Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Geary is provided on an <strong>&ldquo;as is&rdquo;</strong> and <strong>&ldquo;as available&rdquo;</strong> basis without warranties of any kind, express or implied, regarding completeness, accuracy, or fitness for a particular purpose. To the fullest extent permitted by law, Geary’s contributors are not liable for any missed deadlines, academic penalties, fees, or damages arising from reliance on content published here.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms of Service may be updated as Geary evolves. Continued use of the site after updates are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
